Subject: [IMPORTANT] IAS B/Haul Promotion

Oct. 23, 2013

TO : All offices under SINWA
CC : CCB, CCE
FM : WSG


Appreciate your efforts to in crease B/Haul performance.

As you know well,
SINWA RHQ have emphasized continuously that our target for B/Haul performna=
ce is not the given QTA
but above 50% against BSA.
Although we have achieved target against QTA as the below table, Performanc=
e against BSA is barely 42%.
Of course, we know that there are so many restriction to increase performan=
ce such as new service launching,
long holiday, political conditions, loading limitation caused by bottlencek=
 etc.
Nevertheless, we need to do our utmost to achieve our internal target for t=
he remainder of this year.
(above 50% against BSA)

T4, all offices are strongly requested to intensify B/Haul sales activities=
 for the rest of this year.
RHQ will monitor B/Haul performance by office and support offices' request =
as much as possible.


1. B/Haul Performance by Lane (WK 01 ~ 33, Data Source : ALPS-COA)

   [cid:image006.jpg@01CEEAB5.482B23D0]


2. B/Haul Performance by Lane (WK 01 ~ 42, Data Source : ALPS-COA)

   1) Over-performing Lane against internal target (above 50% vs. BSA)
       - CKA, CKI, FIX, ITS, JIE, JIS, JTV
       - Please increase your office's performance with more efforts. (inte=
rnal target : above 120% vs. QTA)

   2) Poor performing Lane against internal target (above 50% vs. BSA)
       - AF1, AAZ, AUS, FMX, ICS, TIX, IFX, NCI, JTE, KIS, PSG, RES, WAX
       - Please try to achieve your office' target QTA preferentially. ((in=
ternal target : above 100% vs. QTA)

       * BKS/HES/KPI/NHS/NTS should be excluded in target lane because of s=
pace restriction caused  by T/S cargo volumes.

   [cid:image007.jpg@01CEEAB5.482B23D0]



